# Optional connection config for `test.sh` — copy to `.env` to point the test at ANY MongoDB with one
# value, without passing a variant folder or a URI each time.
#   cp .env.example .env        # then uncomment ONE option below
# `.env` is gitignored. test.sh uses this only when you DON'T pass a TARGET arg or MONGO_URL.
# (Priority: a URI arg / MONGO_URL > THIS .env > a per-variant .env > parts/defaults 127.0.0.1:27017.)
# The database in a URI is ignored — the test creates + drops its own throwaway database; the user needs
# rights to create/drop a database (the variants' built-in `root` role suffices).

# Option A — a single connection URI:
# MONGO_URL=mongodb://dokandar:yourpassword@127.0.0.1:27017/?authSource=admin&directConnection=true

# Option B — individual parts:
# MONGO_HOST=127.0.0.1
# MONGO_PORT=27017
# MONGO_ROOT_USER=dokandar
# MONGO_ROOT_PASSWORD=yourpassword
# MONGO_AUTHSOURCE=admin

# Image tag used for docker-mode (when no host mongosh). Match the server's major version.
# MONGO_VERSION=7.0
